1
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:13,280
Thank you.

2
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:31,120
Oh

3
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:00,930
Ah!

4
00:02:01,013 --> 00:02:02,137
Gomorrah, what are you doing?

5
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:04,717
You're gonna knock us off if
you keep crashing like that!

6
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:05,630
Whoa!

7
00:02:05,713 --> 00:02:07,322
Maybe he's too injured to go on.

8
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,140
What? No!

9
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,720
Gomorrah can't see!

10
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:17,237
His retinas were damaged
in that last attack.

11
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,150
He's blind!

12
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,420
What's that? Gomorrah!

13
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,953
You can't see anything?

14
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:29,517
It started running like crazy.

15
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,277
Don't just stand there, shoot it!

16
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,637
We gotta stop that thing.

17
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:33,957
We can't let it go any further!

18
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:35,720
Fire the transporter.

19
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:40,237
Gomorrah, don't do this. Please stop.

20
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,997
You're in no shape to go on.

21
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,315
You'll kill yourself.

22
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,537
He said that he made a promise.

23
00:02:47,620 --> 00:02:48,920
To Sodom.

24
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,357
He told Sodom.

25
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:54,220
Leave the rest to me!

26
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:58,540
I'll take on your share and carry
everyone the rest of the way!

27
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:01,130
Gomorrah!

28
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:07,320
They were in its stomach?

29
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,280
I'm full already.

30
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:11,629
Couldn't eat another bite.

31
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,200
Let's take him with us as backup food.

32
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:18,040
Big bro! Come here quick!

33
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:21,458
Some pirates gave Sodom and
Gomorrah a serious beating!

34
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:24,057
Pirates have got a lot of nerve.

35
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,434
Never touch my family!

36
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:32,670
Hey!

37
00:03:32,753 --> 00:03:33,840
Take it easy, you two!

38
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:35,117
You're still injured!

39
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,280
This is no time for a dance party!

40
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,510
Oh!

41
00:03:43,593 --> 00:03:44,537
We're headed straight for a dead end!

42
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:46,267
He'll crash into it and die!

43
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,020
Gomorrah! Stop him!

44
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:50,020
You'll never make it! Stop!

45
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:53,540
Dead end?

46
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,300
I don't see one, do you?

47
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:57,310
Nope.

48
00:03:57,393 --> 00:03:59,076
Can't say I see anything of the sort.

49
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:36,920
It's the courthouse!

50
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,120
He did it! Yeah!

51
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,520
You made it!

52
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:46,140
You wore it!

53
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:52,580
All units, the King Bull carrying
the pirates broke through Block D,

54
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:55,057
and they are now at the Courthouse Plaza.

55
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:58,940
I repeat, the King Bull carrying
the pirates broke through.

56
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,300
Look at this, Fogfreed.

57
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,740
A golden transponder snail.

58
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,737
Having this little gadget is the same as

59
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:14,408
having the authority
to issue a Buster Call.

60
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:17,780
That means I have the same
power as a Navy Admiral,

61
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:20,138
or someone even higher up than that.

62
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,220
Admiral Aokiji entrusted it to me.

63
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:26,049
The question is, if
and when will I use it?

64
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,790
Hmm.

65
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,380
Just you wait.

66
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,617
Once I revive the ancient weapons,

67
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:34,641
this won't just be something
that's on loan to me.

68
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:39,480
I'll carry it of my own accord, along
with the power to control an army.

69
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:49,020
With a single push of a button,
an entire island will disappear.

70
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:53,060
Authority can be a weapon unto itself.

71
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,420
Oh, the power.

72
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:55,700
Team Spandam!

73
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:58,960
That was close!

74
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:00,934
What's wrong with you?

75
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:02,295
Can't you even knock?

76
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,800
I almost accidentally hit the button!

77
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:09,360
I'm terribly sorry, sir, but I'm
afraid we've got an emergency here.

78
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,994
There's an urgent call from
Enies Lobby's main island.

79
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:14,090
Idiots!

80
00:06:14,173 --> 00:06:17,557
If there's an emergency, why didn't
they just call my room directly?

81
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:18,470
What the?

82
00:06:18,553 --> 00:06:20,600
Hey, why is the receiver off the hook?

83
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:21,980
This always happens.

84
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:23,279
Who's responsible?

85
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:27,537
Well, either way, you were saying
something about an emergency, weren't you?

86
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:28,450
Yes, sir.

87
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,270
Spanda.

88
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:47,360
Hey, Miss Robin,

89
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:49,977
it seems we have an urgent report coming

90
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:52,497
in from the Marines
down at the main island.

91
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:57,060
Knowing what it's likely about, I
wouldn't call it an emergency, exactly.

92
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:03,757
Your friends tried their best, but only
managed to take down five of our soldiers.

93
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:06,217
I wonder how they were
ultimately defeated.

94
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,337
Did some of my other men bring them down?

95
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:11,655
Or was it the giant gatekeeping
team of Oimo and Kashi?

96
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,440
So many possibilities.

97
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,897
Why don't we listen to the report?

98
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:19,917
About those idiots who
defied the world government?

99
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,780
and learn their fate together?

100
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,780
You're such a scumbag!

101
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,140
Shut up, you lowlife!

102
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,560
This is Spandam.

103
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,597
I understand you have a report.

104
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,177
Chiefs spawned him, finally!

105
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:36,090
Thank goodness!

106
00:07:36,173 --> 00:07:38,677
I tried your direct line,
but I couldn't get through!

107
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:39,590
I'm...

108
00:07:39,673 --> 00:07:41,059
I'm not really sure where to begin!

109
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,580
Calm down, take it easy!

110
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:45,277
It's the Straw Hats, right?

111
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,600
Yes, what about them?

112
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:48,100
Whoa, hold on!

113
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:51,500
Listen, just pick up from
where your last report ended.

114
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,685
Give me the gritty details,
loudly and clearly!

115
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:57,817
Right, the intruders - Did
you accidentally kill them?

116
00:07:57,900 --> 00:08:00,317
Pity, it's their fault
for being such weaklings!

117
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,757
The intruders consist of about 60 pirates!

118
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:05,097
They've pushed their way
all the way through the

119
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:07,497
main island and have reached
the courthouse plaza.

120
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:09,480
We can't stop them, sir!

121
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:20,300
All personnel on Enies Lobby's main island
head to the courthouse plaza immediately!

122
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:25,680
You did a good job, Gomorrah.

123
00:08:26,060 --> 00:08:30,140
I swear everything you two
did will not be in vain.

124
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,437
All right, we're breaking in!

125
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:36,520
It's time to say big bro breaking!

126
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:37,790
Yeah!

127
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:41,200
I repeat!

128
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:44,186
The Pirates have reached
the Courthouse Plaza!

129
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,660
Can you see Luffy?

130
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,010
Nope.

131
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,477
But whether he's up on the roof or not,

132
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:17,457
it's not exactly like we
can just jump up after him.

133
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:18,370
That's true.

134
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,960
How much we can do.

135
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:23,640
How many members of CP9
did you see up there?

136
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:26,604
It was just that one big
guy with the bullhorns.

137
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:32,482
It's hard to believe that Robin, Franky,
all of them are right behind those doors.

138
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,628
In any case, we need
to catch up with Luffy.

139
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:39,100
Then we can save Robin together! Hurry!

140
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:40,634
Get to the courthouse!

141
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,397
The draw break isn't down yet!

142
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,310
Corner them!

143
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:05,590
Whoa!

144
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:06,856
That frog's awesome!

145
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:09,077
That's the same ball
that took out Gomorrah!

146
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,080
Who threw it?

147
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:14,970
Whoa!

148
00:10:15,053 --> 00:10:15,883
There's three of them!

149
00:10:15,966 --> 00:10:17,297
And they're running away!

150
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:18,817
Why are they running away?

151
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,517
They're the ones that attacked first!

152
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,430
Idiot cook!

153
00:10:21,513 --> 00:10:24,237
We can't go around chasing every
enemy that runs off like that!

154
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,555
It's a waste of time!

155
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,780
Oh, pipe down. It's confirmation.

156
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:48,677
Some of them need to
be chased, understand?

157
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:50,317
To find out who we're up against.

158
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:55,060
Who is this guy?

159
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:58,817
He must have superhuman strength to
swing something like that around.

160
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:01,817
You think he's part of some
special unit like those guard dogs?

161
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:05,077
There are probably more of them
hiding out there somewhere.

162
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:06,200
Let's be careful.

163
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:10,600
We need to get moving.

164
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,097
It looks like the
reinforcements have arrived.

165
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:14,010
Surround them!

166
00:11:14,093 --> 00:11:16,797
There's no way they'll be able
to open those heavy stone doors!

167
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,097
We'll have them cornered!

168
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:19,010
Move it!

169
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,360
He's right.

170
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:23,240
Now that I think about it, how...

171
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:29,680
Are we gonna open those big stones?

172
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,555
We're going in first!

173
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:36,077
Stay close, don't fall behind! He...

174
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:37,760
he cut right through them!

175
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,180
Like it was nothing!

176
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:40,830
Hey, Samba!

177
00:11:40,913 --> 00:11:41,760
Let's split up!

178
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:43,777
We need to charge both of those towers!

179
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:46,617
Because each side has a lever
to open up that drawbridge!

180
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:47,530
Yeah!

181
00:11:47,613 --> 00:11:49,720
Good thinking! I'm on it! Right!

182
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:52,537
Looks like we need to
split into three teams!

183
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:55,437
Most of you go with Kiwi and
Mozu, the rest are with me!

184
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:57,991
We'll crack some heads in that courthouse!

185
00:11:58,140 --> 00:11:59,720
Good luck, everyone! Move!

186
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:02,790
Ahhhhhhh!

187
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:13,690
Huh?

188
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:14,990
Also,

189
00:12:15,073 --> 00:12:17,997
the gatekeepers of the main
island front gate, Oimo and Kashi,

190
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,417
have joined up with the pirates!

191
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:22,757
They're currently destroying the
central part of the main island!

192
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,740
We are the way!

193
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:32,117
After hearing all the field reports,

194
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:35,600
our guard casualties total
must be over 2,000 men!

195
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:37,680
Wait, not five?

196
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:41,637
And the man who took down over
1,000 of those men all by himself,

197
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,817
the notorious Straw Hat Luffy,
has suddenly disappeared!

198
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,312
We're still assessing the situation here!

199
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:52,837
In the history of this island, this is
without a doubt the absolute worst thing?

200
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:55,038
And it never happened in any slobby!

201
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:02,240
It's Bluno.

202
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:05,131
What's he doing out there on that rooftop?

203
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:09,680
What's happening here?

204
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,040
And why now?

205
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,660
What the hell's going on?

206
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:18,370
Baskerville!

207
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:21,617
Chief Justice Baskerville!
Come in! It's me!

208
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:24,020
Oh, hello, Chief Spottom.

209
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:27,040
This is left, Baskerville, on the left.

210
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:29,217
This is right, Baskerville, on the right.

211
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:32,097
And located in the center,
it is none other than I.

212
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:34,180
Central freeway closed for repair.

213
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:35,397
Oh, shut up!

214
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,577
Just give me a status report, dammit!

215
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:41,577
Is it true that the intruders have
made it to the Courthouse Plaza or not?

216
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:42,490
Let's see.

217
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,460
A status report, huh?

218
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:49,720
That's a tricky one.

219
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:54,260
They're not so much in the plaza
as they are inside the courthouse.

220
00:13:54,420 --> 00:13:56,540
It's just awful. What?

221
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:06,820
Chief, Chief Justice, I have a report.

222
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:11,117
The pirates have cut through our
defenses and broken down the front door.

223
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:14,060
They're currently inside the courthouse.

224
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,897
We can see that already, fool.

225
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,156
Not as much resistance as I expected.

226
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,913
We should be able to tear right through.

227
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,030
What's that?

228
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:25,380
Whoa, what?

229
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:26,735
He's got three heads!

230
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:30,660
He's just like that dog that
guards the underworld. Marverous?

231
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,040
You mean Cerberus!

232
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:33,957
Order in the court, damn it!

233
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,805
This is a sacred chamber
of law, you hooligans!

234
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:42,001
You had the nerve to bust in here, so shut
up, sit still, and receive your sentence!

235
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,870
All right, guys.

236
00:14:45,953 --> 00:14:48,800
You head to the roof and
join up with Straw Hat.

237
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:52,937
We'll stay here at the door with
Yokozuna and hold off the Marines.

238
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:57,237
We'll watch your back, so keep moving
and don't worry about the small fries.

239
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,240
You got it.

240
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:01,717
Hey, it looks like they're starting
some kind of trial over there.

241
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,500
Who cares? Just ignore them.

242
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:04,717
Which way do we go?

243
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:05,630
Straight ahead.

244
00:15:05,713 --> 00:15:07,237
There are stairs on both sides.

245
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,897
Let's make our way to the top.

246
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:09,810
Right.

247
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:10,810
Hey!

248
00:15:10,893 --> 00:15:12,057
They're ignoring the trial!

249
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:14,837
I know they're pirates, but seriously,
how rude can these guys get?

250
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:15,800
Bad bastards!

251
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:18,257
How dare you mock the Judicial Island!

252
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:19,987
I'll teach you some respect!

253
00:15:23,180 --> 00:15:25,827
Are his sword spinning
or am I seeing things?

254
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,100
Charming demon.

255
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:30,760
Sleepless knight.

256
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,400
Is he the guy who broke the door?

257
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:50,300
Well that's that now
let's get moving right.

258
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:56,617
He puts all of us to shame and he's
not even the captain of their crew.

259
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:59,697
Hey hey hey wait out of the way reindeer

260
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:02,368
out of the way moss
head i'm coming through.

261
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:07,417
I forgot about him somebody's gotta protect
nami from all these bad guys and that

262
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:13,560
somebody's Gonna be me damn it no watch
it what why is he picking a fight now?

263
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:17,157
If you want to settle this, then bring it!

264
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:18,070
Shut up!

265
00:16:18,153 --> 00:16:21,017
This is your fault for trying
to hog Nami all for yourself!

266
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,041
Follow me, Nami.

267
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,160
Forget about him.

268
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:24,900
Uh, hey.

269
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:27,924
We came to this place to
rescue Robin, remember?

270
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,150
Oh!

271
00:16:29,233 --> 00:16:30,788
I bet she's waiting for me!

272
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,977
She's waiting for her prince to save her!

273
00:16:33,060 --> 00:16:35,817
She's probably crying right now
because she misses me so much!

274
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:36,730
Whatever!

275
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:40,370
Come on!

276
00:16:40,453 --> 00:16:41,496
Are you kidding me?!

277
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:43,760
Come back, Zoro!

278
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:45,097
That's the wrong way!

279
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:46,100
Are you sure?

280
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:50,017
How can you screw this up when the
stairs are right in front of your face?

281
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:51,157
What's wrong with you?

282
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,817
If you stopped giving such crappy
directions, this wouldn't happen.

283
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,724
You are not blaming this on me!

284
00:16:56,680 --> 00:17:01,033
Zoro, I'll try to make you some medicine
later to fix your brain problem.

285
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:02,110
Brain problem?

286
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:05,760
Hey, Chopper, make some
for him while you're at it.

287
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:08,737
I'll try, but he may be beyond help.

288
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:12,157
I'm starting to have doubts
about this whole rescue thing.

289
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:15,137
They'll pull it together when
the going gets tough, I'm sure.

290
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:16,920
I mean, probably.

291
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:19,120
I mean, hopefully.

292
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:22,200
These are serious crimes.

293
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:24,400
Yes, they're quite grave indeed.

294
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:30,000
But we should show restraint and
sentence them to death. Agreed.

295
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:34,940
Think you can ignore
the Chief Justice, huh?

296
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:51,280
Chopper, Nami, go on ahead.

297
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:56,197
I'll make quick work of this thing
and catch up with you in a second.

298
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,110
No!

299
00:17:57,193 --> 00:17:58,700
I'm a thing now, am I?

300
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:00,507
And easy to defeat, no less?

301
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:03,757
I'll teach you the meaning
of fear, you little...

302
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:05,340
Poo!

303
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,460
No, stop it!

304
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:15,660
He-ho-he-he-he!

305
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:30,200
You gotta go through us first, Cerberus.

306
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:31,972
Are you sure about this?

307
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:34,020
Huh. Let's go.

308
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:35,260
Uh, right.

309
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:51,330
Finally!

310
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:53,320
My face closed! Of course.

311
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:56,120
All open doors will eventually shut.

312
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:59,616
I'm amazed you still managed
to dodge my Tempest kick.

313
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,177
Yeah, no big deal.

314
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:02,820
How unsettling.

315
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:07,520
Check!

316
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:11,680
He's fast!

317
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:14,800
Finger pistol!

318
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:16,190
Change!

319
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:18,190
Fire buddy!

320
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,560
How come?

321
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,460
Fire!

322
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:26,020
Buddy!

323
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,460
He's completely keeping up with my speed.

324
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:49,486
He even changed the
course of my Tempest Kick.

325
00:19:49,620 --> 00:19:51,980
His physical abilities are unbelievable.

326
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:55,420
It's no good. Hmm?

327
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,960
I can't stay like this.

328
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,340
It won't work.

329
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:01,680
I lost Aokiji.

330
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:03,520
I realized something.

331
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:05,260
I said to myself,

332
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:08,497
you keep running into guys
that are stronger and stronger,

333
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,462
unless you can get stronger too.

334
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:13,080
You can't protect your friends.

335
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:16,100
And I want to.

336
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:18,037
They're not all strong like me.

337
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:20,997
But either way, they're my
friends and I want to keep them.

338
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:23,609
So I have to get stronger
than anyone else.

339
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:26,837
Otherwise, there's a
chance I could lose them.

340
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:28,685
Then what are you going to do?

341
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:32,320
I thought of a new way to
fight with all my might.

342
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:35,300
So that I won't lose anyone.

343
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:42,040
So I won't let anyone slip away from me.

344
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,557
What's happening to him?

345
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:45,522
What's going on inside his body?

346
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,520
That did it.

347
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:54,160
You won't be able to stop me now What?

348
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:59,460
All my strength and techniques
just went up by one step

349
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,840
Second gear!

350
00:21:40,580 --> 00:21:41,897
Thank

351
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:48,137
you so

352
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:49,460
much for watching.
